WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.074 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson one.

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:05.355 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Introduction.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:07.616 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:09.489 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.061 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information and

00:00:12.061 --> 00:00:14.264 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.164 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:16.684 --> 00:00:18.448 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.448 --> 00:00:20.139 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:20.659 --> 00:00:22.724 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:22.724 --> 00:00:24.434 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.484 --> 00:00:27.540 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.302 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:29.822 --> 00:00:31.889 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A close is the last price of the day.

00:00:33.044 --> 00:00:34.943 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:35.942 --> 00:00:37.918 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end of this series you will

00:00:37.918 --> 00:00:39.968 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
understand what a grid bot, a small

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.017 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
program that places these orders

00:00:42.017 --> 00:00:43.920 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for you, does, when it can capture

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.531 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bounces, and where it loses.

00:00:46.051 --> 00:00:48.061 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will know how to plan one, test

00:00:48.061 --> 00:00:49.961 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it on paper, run it, check it, and

00:00:49.961 --> 00:00:52.008 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
change the capital you give to bots

00:00:52.008 --> 00:00:53.870 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
only under written risk rules.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:55.787 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is education, not

00:00:55.787 --> 00:00:57.106 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a promise of results.

00:00:57.626 --> 00:00:59.237 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Price often moves sideways,

00:00:59.237 --> 00:01:00.987 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bouncing between the same top

00:01:00.987 --> 00:01:02.738 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and bottom instead of leaving.

00:01:03.258 --> 00:01:04.967 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid is a ladder of waiting

00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:06.677 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
orders, called limit orders,

00:01:06.677 --> 00:01:08.164 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
built for that bouncing.

00:01:08.684 --> 00:01:10.528 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
When price runs one way and stays

00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:12.706 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
there, the grid has nothing left to do.

00:01:13.087 --> 00:01:14.763 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
And if price falls through the

00:01:14.763 --> 00:01:16.272 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom, you're left holding

00:01:16.272 --> 00:01:17.612 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin that is worth less.

00:01:18.282 --> 00:01:19.623 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will know

00:01:19.623 --> 00:01:20.908 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
what a grid bot places.

00:01:22.037 --> 00:01:24.116 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will see that idea on

00:01:24.116 --> 00:01:26.091 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
one real path from 2023.

00:01:27.291 --> 00:01:28.799 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will be able to say the

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:30.252 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop rule in one sentence.

00:01:31.205 --> 00:01:33.051 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
When a chart says Example, it

00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:34.897 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
means a real past price used

00:01:34.897 --> 00:01:36.743 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as an example, not a forecast.

00:01:37.793 --> 00:01:39.035 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is a digital

00:01:39.035 --> 00:01:40.432 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
asset, such as bitcoin.

00:01:40.952 --> 00:01:42.628 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not need to have bought

00:01:42.628 --> 00:01:43.913 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
any before this lesson.

00:01:44.291 --> 00:01:46.259 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange is the website or app

00:01:46.259 --> 00:01:48.591 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
where you swap Australian dollars for

00:01:48.591 --> 00:01:50.631 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, and crypto back to dollars.

00:01:51.151 --> 00:01:52.827 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name one,

00:01:52.827 --> 00:01:54.503 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and it does not send an order.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.813 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Cash is money you can spend.

00:01:57.215 --> 00:01:58.837 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here that means dollars, or a

00:01:58.837 --> 00:02:00.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollar-pegged token, treated

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.011 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
like cash in this lesson.

00:02:02.531 --> 00:02:04.723 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Coin is the crypto, such as bitcoin.

00:02:05.773 --> 00:02:08.119 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order is an instruction to buy or sell.

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:10.378 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A buy order swaps cash for coin.

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:13.262 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A sell order swaps coin back to cash, and

00:02:13.262 --> 00:02:15.626 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you can only sell coin you already hold.

00:02:16.676 --> 00:02:18.446 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot is software that places

00:02:18.446 --> 00:02:20.068 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and refills orders for you.

00:02:20.588 --> 00:02:22.432 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You start with some cash and some

00:02:22.432 --> 00:02:24.108 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin, so there is something to

00:02:24.108 --> 00:02:25.839 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy with and something to sell.

00:02:25.888 --> 00:02:28.253 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid bot places waiting buy orders

00:02:28.253 --> 00:02:30.381 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on lines below the price and sell

00:02:30.381 --> 00:02:32.510 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
orders on lines above it, inside a

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:34.244 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
top and a bottom you choose.

00:02:34.764 --> 00:02:36.440 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The space between your top and

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.172 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your bottom is called the band.

00:02:38.281 --> 00:02:40.386 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sells need some coin, so a grid

00:02:40.386 --> 00:02:42.336 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
starts with part cash and part

00:02:42.336 --> 00:02:44.285 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin, and that is a description,

00:02:44.285 --> 00:02:46.157 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not advice about what to hold.

00:02:47.207 --> 00:02:48.913 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A limit order is an order that

00:02:48.913 --> 00:02:50.477 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits at a price you choose.

00:02:50.996 --> 00:02:52.561 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not chase the price.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.544 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Chasing the price would mean

00:02:54.544 --> 00:02:55.997 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
moving the order to follow

00:02:55.997 --> 00:02:57.561 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wherever the price has gone.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.485 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order fills when the price reaches

00:03:00.485 --> 00:03:02.217 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
its line and the trade happens.

00:03:02.679 --> 00:03:04.885 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Until then, the order is only waiting.

00:03:05.935 --> 00:03:07.891 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Think of a ladder leaned on a wall.

00:03:08.032 --> 00:03:10.378 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rungs wait, and they do not chase you.

00:03:10.654 --> 00:03:12.945 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A rung is one price where an order waits.

00:03:13.352 --> 00:03:15.530 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The gap is the space between two rungs.

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:17.864 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The ladder is the analogy, and the

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:20.136 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
chart beside it is the real past path.

00:03:21.186 --> 00:03:22.596 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The range is the top rung

00:03:22.596 --> 00:03:23.725 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the bottom rung.

00:03:24.245 --> 00:03:26.368 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The levels are the rungs between them.

00:03:26.718 --> 00:03:29.008 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop is the written rule for leaving.

00:03:29.857 --> 00:03:31.701 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The range is the top line and the

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:33.545 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom line, taken from the path.

00:03:34.023 --> 00:03:37.248 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart is bitcoin's real daily

00:03:37.248 --> 00:03:40.817 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closes from 19 July to 16 October 2023.

00:03:41.337 --> 00:03:42.790 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every close in this window

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.522 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed between those two lines.

00:03:45.308 --> 00:03:47.713 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six gaps of about 900 dollars each sit

00:03:47.713 --> 00:03:50.275 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the bottom line and the top line.

00:03:50.794 --> 00:03:53.021 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each gap is about 900 dollars:

00:03:53.021 --> 00:03:55.248 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the top line minus the bottom

00:03:55.248 --> 00:03:56.733 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, divided by six.

00:03:57.253 --> 00:03:58.588 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is one step between

00:03:58.588 --> 00:04:00.071 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lines, not the whole band.

00:04:00.591 --> 00:04:02.430 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Seven lines make those six gaps.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:04.738 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The levels are the prices on the

00:04:04.738 --> 00:04:06.414 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
rungs where limit orders wait.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.691 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Buy orders wait on lines below the price.

00:04:10.127 --> 00:04:12.082 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Sell orders wait on lines above it.

00:04:12.563 --> 00:04:15.063 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each fill changes what you hold: a buy

00:04:15.063 --> 00:04:17.729 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fill adds coin, and a sell fill adds cash.

00:04:18.249 --> 00:04:19.366 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You choose the band,

00:04:19.366 --> 00:04:20.651 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the gaps and the money.

00:04:20.935 --> 00:04:22.387 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot places each order.

00:04:23.394 --> 00:04:25.187 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
After a fill, the bot places the

00:04:25.187 --> 00:04:26.908 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
opposite order one rung away.

00:04:27.428 --> 00:04:29.606 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A buy fill gets a sell one rung higher.

00:04:29.993 --> 00:04:32.222 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A sell fill gets a buy one rung lower.

00:04:32.742 --> 00:04:34.363 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You still write the stop, and

00:04:34.363 --> 00:04:36.039 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you act when that rule is met.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:38.505 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot does not decide the stop for you

00:04:38.505 --> 00:04:40.628 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
unless you turned that setting on, and

00:04:40.628 --> 00:04:42.695 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you write which one before you start.

00:04:43.429 --> 00:04:44.770 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Think of a market stall.

00:04:45.202 --> 00:04:47.316 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stallholder buys stock a little

00:04:47.316 --> 00:04:49.430 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cheaper and sells it a little dearer,

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.050 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and pays a fee on every sale.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.228 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid can do that while price

00:04:53.228 --> 00:04:54.668 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bounces inside the band.

00:04:55.188 --> 00:04:57.709 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bounce means price moves down and back

00:04:57.709 --> 00:05:00.078 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
up, or up and back down, and stays inside.

00:05:00.598 --> 00:05:02.834 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One buy at a lower line and the later

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:04.917 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sell of that same coin is one pair.

00:05:05.437 --> 00:05:07.589 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On these daily closes, the July to

00:05:07.589 --> 00:05:09.821 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
October example window finished

00:05:09.821 --> 00:05:11.893 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
only three pairs one rung apart.

00:05:12.413 --> 00:05:14.145 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell line is higher, so the

00:05:14.145 --> 00:05:15.989 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cash that comes back is more than

00:05:15.989 --> 00:05:17.944 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the cash that left, before the fee.

00:05:18.237 --> 00:05:19.690 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A fee is what the exchange

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:21.254 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
charges when an order fills.

00:05:21.435 --> 00:05:23.055 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The fee comes out of the gap.

00:05:23.282 --> 00:05:25.014 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the fees are larger than the

00:05:25.014 --> 00:05:26.578 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gap, the pair keeps nothing.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.002 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is not a promise.

00:05:28.522 --> 00:05:30.326 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair finishes only if price

00:05:30.326 --> 00:05:32.199 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
does bounce and both orders fill.

00:05:33.249 --> 00:05:34.478 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The daily close is the

00:05:34.478 --> 00:05:35.707 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
last price of the day.

00:05:36.128 --> 00:05:37.928 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto trades all day, so the

00:05:37.928 --> 00:05:39.336 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
day is cut at a set time.

00:05:39.856 --> 00:05:42.061 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The daily close is the end of

00:05:42.061 --> 00:05:44.554 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
each UTC day, 11am Sydney time in

00:05:44.554 --> 00:05:47.142 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daylight saving, 10am otherwise.

00:05:47.662 --> 00:05:49.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is a simple candle that shows

00:05:49.646 --> 00:05:51.322 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the day's high, low and close.

00:05:51.795 --> 00:05:53.725 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Traders call it a candle because

00:05:53.725 --> 00:05:55.654 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the full version has a thick body

00:05:55.654 --> 00:05:57.386 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and a thin wick, like a candle.

00:05:57.818 --> 00:05:59.326 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here we only need the high,

00:05:59.326 --> 00:06:00.555 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the low and the close.

00:06:00.889 --> 00:06:04.068 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This candle is 19 July 2023.

00:06:04.588 --> 00:06:05.817 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The high, the low, and

00:06:05.817 --> 00:06:07.102 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the close are labelled.

00:06:07.995 --> 00:06:10.124 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The example is Bitcoin's public

00:06:10.124 --> 00:06:11.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily price in US dollars.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:15.499 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
From 19 July 2023 to 16 October

00:06:15.499 --> 00:06:18.442 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2023, every one of those days

00:06:18.442 --> 00:06:20.873 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closed inside the band.

00:06:21.393 --> 00:06:23.066 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The close crossed the seven

00:06:23.066 --> 00:06:24.812 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lines 28 times in that window.

00:06:25.332 --> 00:06:27.644 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The count is an example, not a forecast.

00:06:28.164 --> 00:06:29.952 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
We do not need to read each day.

00:06:30.218 --> 00:06:31.560 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The shape is the lesson,

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:32.974 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and it is marked Example.

00:06:33.494 --> 00:06:36.250 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: 19 July

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.330 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2023 to 16 October 2023.

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:41.359 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The low is the bottom line.

00:06:41.839 --> 00:06:43.305 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The high is the top line.

00:06:43.825 --> 00:06:45.669 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nothing on this card is an order.

00:06:46.632 --> 00:06:49.566 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Those 28 crossings are not 28 results.

00:06:50.086 --> 00:06:52.288 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A crossing only means the close moved

00:06:52.288 --> 00:06:54.355 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
from one side of a line to the other.

00:06:54.797 --> 00:06:56.508 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A pair is finished only when a

00:06:56.508 --> 00:06:58.362 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy and its later sell have both

00:06:58.362 --> 00:07:00.094 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled, and only after the fee.

00:07:00.594 --> 00:07:02.493 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The price can cross many lines and

00:07:02.493 --> 00:07:04.392 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
still leave you holding coin if it

00:07:04.392 --> 00:07:06.012 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
walks out through the bottom.

00:07:06.549 --> 00:07:08.057 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You can buy part of a coin.

00:07:08.606 --> 00:07:11.566 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here we buy one hundredth

00:07:11.607 --> 00:07:12.668 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of a bitcoin, 0.01.

00:07:12.668 --> 00:07:15.632 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example a buy waiting at the

00:07:15.632 --> 00:07:18.921 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lower of these two lines was reached on

00:07:18.921 --> 00:07:21.902 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
17 August 2023, and the sell one line

00:07:21.902 --> 00:07:24.883 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
above was reached on 29 August 2023.

00:07:25.403 --> 00:07:27.191 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The card shows the gap, then the

00:07:27.191 --> 00:07:28.755 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
two fees, then what is left.

00:07:29.064 --> 00:07:30.888 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That is about 8 dollars 46

00:07:30.888 --> 00:07:32.974 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after fees, for one small pair.

00:07:33.494 --> 00:07:35.393 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It happens only if the price comes

00:07:35.393 --> 00:07:37.069 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
back up through the sell line.

00:07:37.173 --> 00:07:38.905 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the price leaves through the

00:07:38.905 --> 00:07:40.693 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom, you still hold the coin,

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:42.257 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the pair never finishes.

00:07:42.449 --> 00:07:44.237 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This card is not money you made.

00:07:44.635 --> 00:07:46.981 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past results don't predict future results.

00:07:53.969 --> 00:07:55.757 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now watch what you hold when the

00:07:55.757 --> 00:07:57.768 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price leaves the band and stays out.

00:07:58.032 --> 00:07:59.652 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Above the band the sells have

00:07:59.652 --> 00:08:01.439 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you are holding cash,

00:08:01.439 --> 00:08:02.892 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with nothing left to sell.

00:08:03.296 --> 00:08:04.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Below the band the buys have

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:06.313 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you are holding

00:08:06.313 --> 00:08:08.045 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin, with nothing left to buy.

00:08:08.327 --> 00:08:09.719 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That is why the way down

00:08:09.719 --> 00:08:11.478 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
matters most: every buy fills,

00:08:11.478 --> 00:08:13.236 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you are left holding coin.

00:08:15.286 --> 00:08:17.521 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here is that stop rule on the real path.

00:08:17.942 --> 00:08:20.302 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It triggers if a daily close is outside

00:08:20.302 --> 00:08:22.589 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the band, through the top or the bottom,

00:08:22.589 --> 00:08:25.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still outside.

00:08:25.618 --> 00:08:27.070 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then the idea is finished.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.544 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot, which cancels the

00:08:29.544 --> 00:08:31.414 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waiting orders, and do what you

00:08:31.414 --> 00:08:33.507 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wrote: keep the coin or swap to cash.

00:08:34.027 --> 00:08:36.009 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot's automatic stop is a price

00:08:36.009 --> 00:08:37.697 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that can fire during the day.

00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:39.917 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course uses the two daily

00:08:39.917 --> 00:08:41.752 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closes, unless your written plan

00:08:41.752 --> 00:08:43.540 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
says you turned on a price stop.

00:08:43.972 --> 00:08:45.312 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is a teaching rule,

00:08:45.312 --> 00:08:46.490 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not a recommendation.

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:48.630 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop is your written rule

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.083 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for when you stop the bot.

00:08:50.316 --> 00:08:52.449 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On 23 October 2023 the close

00:08:52.449 --> 00:08:54.861 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
finished above the top line, and

00:08:54.861 --> 00:08:57.181 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the next day was still above it.

00:09:02.231 --> 00:09:03.683 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Through the top, the sells

00:09:03.683 --> 00:09:05.359 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
have filled and you hold cash.

00:09:05.468 --> 00:09:07.312 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Through the bottom, the buys have

00:09:07.312 --> 00:09:09.155 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you hold coin that you

00:09:09.155 --> 00:09:11.166 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bought above where the price is now.

00:09:11.525 --> 00:09:12.978 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That loss can keep growing

00:09:12.978 --> 00:09:14.095 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
until the stop acts.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.244 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot either way, then

00:09:16.244 --> 00:09:17.808 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you follow the written rule.

00:09:17.917 --> 00:09:19.705 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot does not decide the stop

00:09:19.705 --> 00:09:21.604 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
unless you turned that setting on.

00:09:21.877 --> 00:09:23.298 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
EXAMPLE, made up: three

00:09:23.298 --> 00:09:24.878 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buys fill on the way down.

00:09:25.398 --> 00:09:27.975 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One hundredth of a bitcoin at the

00:09:27.975 --> 00:09:30.266 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
middle line is 276 dollars 30.

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:36.654 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One hundredth at 26,730 is 267 dollars 30.

00:09:37.506 --> 00:09:42.688 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One hundredth at 25,830 is 258 dollars 30.

00:09:43.208 --> 00:09:45.848 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Together that is 801 dollars 90.

00:09:46.368 --> 00:09:48.543 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A little below the band, at a

00:09:48.543 --> 00:09:50.917 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
made-up price of 24,000, that

00:09:50.917 --> 00:09:52.994 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin is worth 720 dollars.

00:09:53.514 --> 00:09:55.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are down 81 dollars 90

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:57.076 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
before fees, and the loss keeps

00:09:57.076 --> 00:09:58.935 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
growing until your stop acts.

00:09:59.985 --> 00:10:01.560 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A common mistake is thinking

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:03.068 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot predicts the price.

00:10:03.857 --> 00:10:04.607 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not.

00:10:05.173 --> 00:10:05.955 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It only waits.

00:10:06.325 --> 00:10:07.833 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Another mistake is starting

00:10:07.833 --> 00:10:09.006 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with no written stop.

00:10:09.421 --> 00:10:10.650 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
There is no promise of

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:11.935 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
results in this lesson.

00:10:12.126 --> 00:10:13.734 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Numbers marked Example are

00:10:13.734 --> 00:10:15.412 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
teaching numbers, not advice.

00:10:16.462 --> 00:10:18.854 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or demo trading is like driving

00:10:18.854 --> 00:10:20.938 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with L-plates: you practise with

00:10:20.938 --> 00:10:23.408 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
pretend money before anything is real.

00:10:23.928 --> 00:10:25.445 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 7 shows you how.

00:10:26.501 --> 00:10:27.629 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Steps one to six.

00:10:28.329 --> 00:10:30.016 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This introduction is step one.

00:10:30.716 --> 00:10:31.778 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then what you need.

00:10:32.408 --> 00:10:33.935 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then exactly what a grid

00:10:33.935 --> 00:10:35.386 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot does, order by order.

00:10:36.386 --> 00:10:37.503 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then market regimes.

00:10:38.079 --> 00:10:40.146 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then choosing grid spacing and range.

00:10:40.786 --> 00:10:42.392 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then entry and exit rules.

00:10:43.108 --> 00:10:44.407 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Steps seven to eleven.

00:10:45.107 --> 00:10:46.192 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then a paper test.

00:10:46.912 --> 00:10:47.974 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then weekly checks.

00:10:48.711 --> 00:10:49.899 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then common mistakes.

00:10:50.599 --> 00:10:52.611 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then scaling up under written rules.

00:10:53.071 --> 00:10:54.462 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then an opt-in lesson on

00:10:54.462 --> 00:10:56.548 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
liquidation and your complete plan.

00:10:57.598 --> 00:10:59.497 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The next lesson is a checklist you

00:10:59.497 --> 00:11:01.397 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
write on paper, before any screen.

00:11:02.418 --> 00:11:04.795 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In short: a grid waits, it buys lower and

00:11:04.795 --> 00:11:07.172 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sells higher while price bounces, the

00:11:07.172 --> 00:11:09.472 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fees come out of the gap, and if a daily

00:11:09.472 --> 00:11:11.926 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close leaves and stays out, you stop the

00:11:11.926 --> 00:11:13.996 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot and follow the rule you wrote.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:15.946 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check yourself.

00:11:16.466 --> 00:11:17.919 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Why does a grid start with

00:11:17.919 --> 00:11:19.371 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
some coin as well as cash?

00:11:19.534 --> 00:11:20.819 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Because the sell orders

00:11:20.819 --> 00:11:22.328 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
need coin you already hold.

00:11:23.346 --> 00:11:26.067 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the example pair, why is the net about

00:11:26.067 --> 00:11:28.363 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
8 dollars 46 and not the whole gap?

00:11:28.883 --> 00:11:30.447 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The two fees come out first.

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:33.677 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Price closes above your top line, and

00:11:33.677 --> 00:11:35.856 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the next day's close is still above it.

00:11:36.163 --> 00:11:37.951 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What do you do, and who does it?

00:11:38.272 --> 00:11:40.059 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot and follow your

00:11:40.059 --> 00:11:41.903 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
written rule, by hand, unless you

00:11:41.903 --> 00:11:43.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
turned on the bot's stop setting.

00:11:44.803 --> 00:11:45.553 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Your turn.

00:11:45.999 --> 00:11:47.731 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On paper, write the top and the

00:11:47.731 --> 00:11:49.687 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom, one gap, and the stop rule.

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.522 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Say what you will do if a daily

00:11:52.522 --> 00:11:54.142 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close leaves the band and the

00:11:54.142 --> 00:11:55.706 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
next close is still outside.

00:11:56.037 --> 00:11:57.434 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Pause the video and write

00:11:57.434 --> 00:11:59.054 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your answer before you go on.

00:12:00.087 --> 00:12:02.154 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No real order is sent in this lesson.

00:12:02.641 --> 00:12:04.544 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper practice comes in Lesson

00:12:04.544 --> 00:12:06.154 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
7, and real money only after

00:12:06.154 --> 00:12:07.984 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your written graduation rule.

00:12:08.504 --> 00:12:10.511 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A graduation rule is the written

00:12:10.511 --> 00:12:12.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
test you pass on paper first.

00:12:12.753 --> 00:12:13.762 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You draw the idea.

00:12:14.282 --> 00:12:16.076 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a screen appears later, it

00:12:16.076 --> 00:12:17.791 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
should be a copy of the page,

00:12:17.791 --> 00:12:19.351 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and only on paper or demo.

00:12:20.551 --> 00:12:22.912 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring a notebook, and no secrets: no

00:12:22.912 --> 00:12:25.526 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
seed phrase, private key or API secret.

00:12:26.046 --> 00:12:27.903 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Those are the words or keys that

00:12:27.903 --> 00:12:29.617 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
unlock a wallet or an account.

00:12:30.667 --> 00:12:32.359 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair, in the next lesson,

00:12:32.359 --> 00:12:33.974 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is the two things you swap,

00:12:33.974 --> 00:12:35.744 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
like bitcoin and US dollars.

00:12:36.794 --> 00:12:38.627 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid bot places waiting buys

00:12:38.627 --> 00:12:40.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
below the price and waiting sells

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:42.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
above it, inside a band you choose.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:44.977 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A finished pair buys

00:12:44.977 --> 00:12:46.262 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lower and sells higher.

00:12:46.469 --> 00:12:48.089 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The fees come out of the gap.

00:12:48.378 --> 00:12:50.436 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the example that was about 8

00:12:50.436 --> 00:12:52.658 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars 46, and it is not a promise.

00:12:53.858 --> 00:12:55.255 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave through the top and

00:12:55.255 --> 00:12:56.428 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you hold mostly cash.

00:12:56.877 --> 00:12:58.218 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave through the bottom

00:12:58.218 --> 00:12:59.615 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you hold mostly coin.

00:13:00.656 --> 00:13:02.894 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a daily close leaves the band and the

00:13:02.894 --> 00:13:04.991 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
next close is still outside, you stop

00:13:04.991 --> 00:13:07.114 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot and follow the rule you wrote.

00:13:08.289 --> 00:13:10.524 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: What you are going to need.

00:13:10.912 --> 00:13:12.477 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your band,

00:13:12.477 --> 00:13:14.097 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:15.727 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example on

00:13:15.727 --> 00:13:17.017 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every practice figure.

00:13:17.537 --> 00:13:19.493 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will write the page

00:13:19.493 --> 00:13:21.504 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of what you need, before any screen.

